LikeOS has neither O_PATH descriptors nor direct (cache-bypassing) I/O.
The symlink-free open helper reports its O_PATH based verification as
unavailable (ENOSYS), as it does on every other system without O_PATH, and
the loop device code opens a backing file for ordinary I/O when direct I/O
is asked for (there are no loop devices on LikeOS, so that path is not
reached by the disk tools).

